<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows $142.3 mln on June 11.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows $142.3 mln on June 11.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $142.3 million deficit on June 11 in the commercial forex market, according to the Central Bank.</p>
<p>The Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON JUNE 11</p>
<p>Exports: $181.3 million</p>
<p>Imports: $276.9 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $480.7 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $527.4 million</p>
<p>Net deficit: $142.3 million</p>
<p>JUNE DOLLAR FLOWS UPDATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.802 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $2.082 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $3.238 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.915 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $43 million</p>
<p>Note: Figures rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo Newsroom, 55 11 2485418))</p>
</text>
